From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the window on a console tells views it is active

A desktop came up on a bare tty with all fourteen input devices live --
`took input device 13:64 (/dev/input/event0), live; holding 1` through
`holding 14`, no revoke, no force pause, no refused open -- and answered
no key at all.

So the descriptors are not the problem any more, and what is left is
where the events go. `DrmWindowHost::CanDispatchEvent` returns true for
every key event, `DispatchEvent` hands it to
`PlatformWindowDelegate::DispatchEvent`, and there it stops: nothing in
the widget has focus, so there is nothing to deliver a key to.

ACTIVATION IS A FACT THE PLATFORM REPORTS UPWARD, AND THIS ONE NEVER
DOES. `WaylandWindow` reports it from `xdg_toplevel.configure`'s
activated state; `X11Window` reports it from `WM_TAKE_FOCUS`.
`DrmWindowHost::Show()` was `visible_ = true;` and nothing else, and
`DrmWindowHost::Activate()` was `NOTIMPLEMENTED_LOG_ONCE()` -- which in
the shipped engine is silence, because `is_debug = false` compiles
`DLOG` out. So a desktop whose keyboard did nothing said nothing about
it anywhere.

This is the ChromeOS gap this series keeps finding, in the same shape as
the DRM master one: ozone/drm's only upstream consumer is ash, ash
decides activation itself through its own `ActivationClient`, and it
never asks the platform window. A views browser is not ash.
`DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::is_active_` starts false and only
`OnActivationChanged` moves it; that call is what reaches
`DesktopNativeWidgetAura::HandleActivationChanged`, which is what calls
`FocusManager::RestoreFocusedView`. Without it no view is ever focused
and every key event dispatched into the tree is dropped -- a desktop
that draws, follows the pointer, and cannot be typed into.

`Show(inactive)` now says so, honoring `inactive` because that is
`Widget`'s own word for "show this without giving it focus"; `Activate`
and `Deactivate` say so on demand; `Hide` withdraws it. `SetActive`
guards on the change rather than the call, because the delegate acts on
every call -- it reorders `open_windows()` and restores focus on the way
to its own early return -- so a repeated deactivation on a window being
torn down is work on a half-destroyed host.

AND THE FIRST EVENT OF EACH KIND IS NAMED IN THE LOG. Everything under
`DispatchEvent` is silent on success: a converter that opened, started
and read logs nothing, and neither does one that opened, started and
never read a byte. Two lines, once each, separate "the descriptors are
dead" from "the events arrive and something above drops them". Those are
two entirely different bugs, and reading the silence as the first one
cost two wrong diagnoses. Per kind rather than per event, because a
trackpad is thousands of events a second and a log nobody can read
answers nothing either.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM. The gap is verified from the sources at the
pin; that it is the whole of why this desktop answers no key is not, and
the two log lines above are there to say so on the next run.
---
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc | 75 ++++++++++++++++++-
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h  | 15 ++++
 2 files changed, 88 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc
index e7ca5f8531aa..f0f0412801fc 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc
@@ -4,7 +4,10 @@
 
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h"
 
+#include <utility>
+
 #include "base/functional/bind.h"
+#include "base/logging.h"
 #include "base/memory/scoped_refptr.h"
 #include "base/notimplemented.h"
 #include "ui/base/cursor/platform_cursor.h"
@@ -71,10 +74,32 @@ gfx::Rect DrmWindowHost::GetCursorConfinedBounds() const {
 
 void DrmWindowHost::Show(bool inactive) {
   visible_ = true;
+
+  // THE WINDOW SAYS IT IS ACTIVE, BECAUSE NOTHING ELSE WILL. Activation is a
+  // fact the platform reports upward -- `WaylandWindow` from
+  // `xdg_toplevel.configure`'s activated state, `X11Window` from
+  // `WM_TAKE_FOCUS` -- and ozone/drm reports it never, for the reason it
+  // NOTREACHED()s half of this interface: ash is its only consumer, and ash
+  // decides activation itself through its own `ActivationClient` without ever
+  // asking the platform window.
+  //
+  // A views browser is not ash. `DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::is_active_`
+  // starts false and only `OnActivationChanged` moves it, and that call is
+  // what reaches `DesktopNativeWidgetAura::HandleActivationChanged` ->
+  // `FocusManager::RestoreFocusedView`. Without it no view in the widget ever
+  // holds focus, so the key events this class dispatches arrive at a window
+  // tree with nothing focused to deliver them to and are dropped -- a desktop
+  // that draws, tracks the pointer, and answers no key at all.
+  //
+  // `inactive` is `Widget`'s own word for "show this without giving it
+  // focus", and it is honored for the same reason the rest of this class
+  // answers rather than asserts: it is what the caller asked for.
+  SetActive(!inactive);
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::Hide() {
   visible_ = false;
+  SetActive(false);
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::Close() {
@@ -250,11 +275,40 @@ PlatformWindowState DrmWindowHost::GetPlatformWindowState() const {
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::Activate() {
-  NOTIMPLEMENTED_LOG_ONCE();
+  // Upstream is `NOTIMPLEMENTED_LOG_ONCE()`, which in the shipped engine --
+  // `is_debug = false`, so `DLOG` is compiled out -- is silence. A desktop
+  // whose keyboard does nothing said nothing about it anywhere.
+  //
+  // THERE IS ONE WINDOW ON A CONSOLE, so activating is telling views what is
+  // already true rather than choosing between candidates. When there is more
+  // than one, the one asked to activate is the one that should be active, and
+  // `SetActive` below is where any deactivation of the others would go.
+  SetActive(true);
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::Deactivate() {
-  NOTIMPLEMENTED_LOG_ONCE();
+  SetActive(false);
+}
+
+void DrmWindowHost::SetActive(bool active) {
+  // GUARDED, BECAUSE THE DELEGATE ACTS ON THE CALL AND NOT ON THE CHANGE.
+  // `DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::OnActivationChanged` returns early when
+  // the state matches, but on the way there it reorders `open_windows()` and
+  // `DesktopNativeWidgetAura::HandleActivationChanged` restores focus -- so a
+  // repeated activation is work, and a repeated deactivation on a window that
+  // is being torn down is work on a half-destroyed host. `Show` and
+  // `Activate` both land here, and on a startup that calls both, one of them
+  // is a no-op.
+  if (active_ == active) {
+    return;
+  }
+  active_ = active;
+
+  VLOG(1) << "domicile: the window on this console is "
+          << (active ? "active" : "not active")
+          << "; a views browser gives no view focus until it hears this";
+
+  delegate_->OnActivationChanged(active);
 }
 
 void DrmWindowHost::SetUseNativeFrame(bool use_native_frame) {}
@@ -352,6 +406,23 @@ bool DrmWindowHost::CanDispatchEvent(const PlatformEvent& event) {
 uint32_t DrmWindowHost::DispatchEvent(const PlatformEvent& event) {
   DCHECK(event);
 
+  // SAID ONCE PER KIND, AND THAT IS THE POINT. Whether a desktop that answers
+  // nothing is reading its devices at all is the first question about it, and
+  // the layers below this one are silent on success: a converter that opened,
+  // started and read logs nothing, and neither does a converter that opened,
+  // started and never read a byte. One line per kind of event separates "the
+  // descriptors are dead" from "the events arrive and something above drops
+  // them", which is two entirely different bugs and was two wrong diagnoses.
+  //
+  // Per kind rather than per event because a trackpad is thousands of events
+  // a second and a log nobody can read answers nothing either.
+  if (event->IsKeyEvent() && !std::exchange(said_a_key_arrived_, true)) {
+    VLOG(1) << "domicile: the first key event reached the window";
+  } else if (event->IsLocatedEvent() &&
+             !std::exchange(said_a_pointer_arrived_, true)) {
+    VLOG(1) << "domicile: the first pointer event reached the window";
+  }
+
   if (event->IsLocatedEvent()) {
     // Make the event location relative to this window's origin.
     LocatedEvent* located_event = event->AsLocatedEvent();
diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h
index 916342495552..a0d9a09cf623 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h
@@ -111,6 +111,11 @@ class DrmWindowHost : public PlatformWindow,
   // on, which on this platform is the whole of a CRTC.
   gfx::Rect FullscreenBounds(int64_t target_display_id) const;
 
+  // Tells views this window is (or is no longer) the active one, once per
+  // change. Ozone/DRM is the only platform with nothing to read this off, so
+  // it is the only one that has to decide it.
+  void SetActive(bool active);
+
   const raw_ptr<PlatformWindowDelegate> delegate_;        // Not owned.
   const raw_ptr<GpuThreadAdapter> sender_;                // Not owned.
   const raw_ptr<EventFactoryEvdev> event_factory_;        // Not owned.
@@ -127,6 +132,16 @@ class DrmWindowHost : public PlatformWindow,
   // methods a views browser asks for during startup, because ash never asks
   // them on ChromeOS. These are what two of the answers need.
   bool visible_ = false;
+  // What this window last told views about its activation. Upstream tells it
+  // nothing ever, which leaves `DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::is_active_`
+  // false for the life of the process and every view in the widget unfocused
+  // -- a desktop that draws and answers no key.
+  bool active_ = false;
+  // Whether the first event of each kind has been named in the log. A desktop
+  // that answers nothing needs to say whether events reach it at all, and
+  // everything under this line is silent when it works.
+  bool said_a_key_arrived_ = false;
+  bool said_a_pointer_arrived_ = false;
   std::optional<gfx::Rect> restored_bounds_;
   // What this window last told views it is. Upstream answers kUnknown forever,
   // which makes DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::IsFullscreen() permanently
